30:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-14","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg mb-6","children":"Common questions"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"Does page speed actually affect conversion rates?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Yes, directly. Google's data shows a 1-second delay in mobile load time reduces conversion rate by up to 20%. The mechanism is abandonment - mobile visitors on variable connections leave pages that take over 3 seconds to show content. The CTA doesn't matter if the visitor left before it loaded."}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"What is LCP and why is it the most important speed metric for landing pages?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"LCP (Largest Contentful Paint) measures when the largest visible element - usually the hero image or headline - finishes loading. It's the proxy for 'when did the visitor see something useful'. Google's threshold is 2.5s. Pages above that threshold are penalized in Quality Score for paid ads and in organic rankings."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"What is a normal HTML payload size for a marketing landing page?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Under 120KB for a marketing landing page. Pages regularly exceed this with inline JSON (product data, pricing tables), server-rendered component trees, and injected script payloads. Calendly's homepage HTML is 1.2MB - 10x the heuristic. The audit measures and reports the raw HTML payload size from the fetched source."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"How do third-party scripts affect landing page speed?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Each third-party script (ad pixel, chat widget, review aggregator, A/B test framework) adds a DNS lookup, a connection, and a script execution. Loading four synchronously in the head can add 800ms-2s before the page begins rendering. The fix is to load non-critical scripts asynchronously or defer them after first contentful paint."}]]}],["$","div","4",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"What is Cumulative Layout Shift and why does it hurt conversion?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"CLS measures how much the page layout shifts while loading. When images load without declared width/height attributes, they collapse to zero height and then expand - pushing content down as they load. A visitor targeting the CTA button clicks on something else because the button moved. Google's CLS threshold is 0.1."}]]}]]}]]}]
